{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Aqil ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Ja'far (r.a.)",
  "data": "At the graves of Aqil and Abdullah ibn Ja'far in al-Baqi, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَنَا يَا عَقِيْلَ بْنَ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDANAA YAA A'QEELABNA ABEE TAALIB\nPeace be upon you, O our master, O Aqil, son of Abu Talib.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ عَمِّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA A'MMI RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ عَمِّ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA A'MMI NABIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O cousin of the Prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ عَمِّ حَبِيْبِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA A'MMI HABEEBILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O cousin of the beloved of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ عَمِّ الْمُصْطَفٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA A'MMIL MUSTAFAA\nPeace be upon you, O cousin of the Chosen One.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَخَا عَلِيٍّ الْمُرْتَضٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AKHAA A'LIYYINIL MURTADAA\nPeace be upon you, O brother of Ali al-Murtada.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ الطَّيَّارِ فِي الْجِنَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA A'BDILLAAHIBNI JA'FARINIT TAYYAARI FIL JINAAN\nPeace be upon Abdullah, son of Ja'far, who flies in the gardens of Paradise,\nوَعَلٰى مَنْ حَوْلَكُمَا مِنْ اَصْحَابِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nWA A'LAA MAN HAWLAKUMAA MIN AS-HAABI RASOOLILLAAH\nand upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah who lie around you both.\nرَضِيَ اللّٰهُ تَعَالٰى عَنْكُمْ وَاَرْضَاكُمْ اَحْسَنَ الرِّضَا\nRADIYALLAAHU TA'AALAA A'NKUM WA ARDAAKUM AHSANAR RIDAA\nMay Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with you all and make you pleased in the best way,\nوَجَعَلَ الْجَنَّةَ مَنْزِلَكُمْ وَمَسْكَنَكُمْ وَمَحَلَّكُمْ وَمَاْوَاكُمْ\nWA JA'ALAL JANNATA MANZILAKUM WA MASKANAKUM WA MAHALLAKUM WA MA'WAAKUM\nand make Paradise your dwelling, your home, your station and your shelter.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you all, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "Aqil, son of Abu Talib, was a brother of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) and of Ja'far al-Tayyar, and the father of Muslim ibn Aqeel (a.s.). He died in Madinah in the late fifties AH. Abdullah, son of Ja'far al-Tayyar, was the husband of Lady Zainab (s.a.); his sons Awn and Muhammad were martyred with Imam Husayn (a.s.) at Karbala. He died in Madinah in 80 AH (or 84). Both are buried in al-Baqi.\n\nThis ziyarat is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, without a narrated source."
}
